<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Patina</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 BCE – 738 BCE (approx.) · capital Kunulua</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Patina, a Neo-Hittite kingdom of the Amuq plain whose founder called it Palistin, a name that may link it to the Philistines.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age-collapse">Late Bronze Age collapse</a>, a kingdom arose in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amuq-valley">Amuq plain</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antakya</a>, the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mukish">Kingdom of Mukish</a>. Inscriptions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taita">King Taita</a>, found in the temple of the storm god at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, call it Palistin, and its capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-tayinat">Kunulua</a>, at Tell Tayinat.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings wrote Luwian hieroglyphic inscriptions and built palaces and temples in Syrian-Hittite style; a temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-tayinat">Tell Tayinat</a> yielded an Assyrian treaty tablet. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> called the land Pattin or Unqi. It lived from the fertile plain and the route to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Patina paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurnasirpal-ii">Ashurnasirpal II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>. After King Tutammu rebelled, Tiglath-Pileser III captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-tayinat">Kunulua</a> in 738 BCE and made the land an Assyrian province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/patina.jpg" alt="Patina" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: w:User:Micahmn · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minneapolis_City_Hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 BCE – 738 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kunulua</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Taita, Lubarna, Tutammu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Luwian and Syrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian, Aramaic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Unqi, Pattin, Palistin</dd></dl></aside></div>

